---
description: Plan HyperFrames films in this Cursor chat, then render with BAML
alwaysApply: true
---

When asked for a video, write one `FilmPlan` story that matches `baml_src/film.baml` and run `baml run main -- --plan_file videos/<slug>/plan.json`. That writes two video plans from the same story. `preview-plan.json` is the cheap cut: a still avatar and a local Kokoro TTS voice (`af_heart` unless the plan says otherwise). `production-plan.json` is the HeyGen lip-sync avatar. Its `voice_id` is the speaking voice and is often not that avatar's default voice. Set it explicitly. Do not leave it blank, and do not copy the avatar id into it. Render only the preview: `baml run render_cut -- --dir videos/<slug> --cut preview`. Then stop for a person to review that cut. Do not call HeyGen, do not ask for an API key, and do not render the production cut. After the person approves in chat, run `baml run approve -- --dir videos/<slug>`. Republishing the story deletes `approval.json`. The subscription model in this chat is the planner.
